Root cause:
The bug was caused by platform-specific code in the NativeIO.c file that was not properly guarded against compilation on non-UNIX platforms, leading to compilation errors on Windows after changes made in HADOOP-7824. The initialization of Java constants that are specific to UNIX was being included in the build for Windows, which is not compatible.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
SET_INT_OR_RETURN(env, clazz, S_IXUSR);
```
Reason:
This line initializes a Java constant `S_IXUSR`, which is specific to UNIX platforms. Since this code is not guarded by any preprocessor directives, it gets included in the compilation for Windows, leading to errors because `S_IXUSR` is not defined in that environment.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
#ifdef UNIX
SET_INT_OR_RETURN(env, clazz, S_IXUSR);
#endif
```
Reason:
By wrapping the initialization of the UNIX-specific constant `S_IXUSR` with `#ifdef UNIX`, the code ensures that this line is only compiled when the target platform is UNIX. This prevents compilation errors on Windows, thus fixing the bug.


